<description>&lt;p&gt;Russia is expanding its military presence in Libya while Turkey is deepening its security strategy, both adding new foreign forces to the conflict. The Libyan leadership transition continues, with the military seizing narcotics after a firefight with smugglers and an explosion at a Misrata munitions depot prompting renewed scrutiny of political decisions by Dbeibah and Zoubi. Haftar has pledged support to Syrian forces, and GECOL is training Libyan technicians in Germany for the Tripoli power plant, indicating ongoing state capacity building. The oil marketing firm in Brega denies any fuel supply failure to the south. According to UCDP, there were two battle-related deaths in 2024.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMibkFVX3lxTE5LMkVoN2dZUFM2SDk4Rm9CcFdUclk0MmtwZ1FyR1QzdXdYRTVQdzhXVHUtQk9zanp5U0QtZ2Z0ejhocTdXVGJ4bXNHZXlUYUZTeDZQOTY2RHZ6TXFSMnRnbFNheURsLVZaaVloNUJB?oc=5&quot;&gt;TheCable&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiUEFVX3lxTE9RY003MDN5V2FLZzA5bUNWd1BBYk5faXd0U0dOT200MVR5Q1VBLVVnLXphajdlZmVlU0dYYTVjZWFzUkU3Ml84Z2NkTk9CMy1Q?oc=5&quot;&gt;سانا&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihgFBVV95cUxQUjZSREpHSGRIVFhyaUNLYTF5bGIwd0dhVHBHcFZtallnd1pBbjZId2FkN1o0VGpMVTlmRkZlcWFoenBPOXhGdV9HcE1rVUZRaUNTVDhfRnBCNlIwR1VRTVg2X1d4TFYwaTcyanpOUUNoUWRwODlHVkdBYURQaEthdGswbmFoZw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Defence24.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqAFBVV95cUxNdW1KSl9acHFoSnM0VVVrN1BIcVBRRFFEZzlRMjNqRHhXNVhsUUg4bEpvU0ZhVFZRY0E1NnhNSGtiMDA5NnVjeHpEYmlWZUZDRkpXb2hESWs2bkhxR0RjYkVvZUJza0xNUG8tbkk3QXFYYUtzc3pVQUhEQS1YSGZyOUJoZjE3c0pzdWs5dm1vVkhRWElydEdGV3RjaDZJZnpqSWd0aHU1QzI?oc=5&quot;&gt;India's News.Net&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiiAFBVV95cUxNODVzVi1iNGhsNVRibWJVYmRmcjNVbz